SUMMARY:A reduction from Hawk to the principal ideal problem in a quaternion algebra
DESCRIPTION:Hawk is a signature published in 2023\, whose security is based on a variant of the Lattice Isomorphism Problem\, called module-LIP. The publication of this signature sparked an interest in the resolution of module-LIP. In this talk\, we present a polynomial time reduction from this problem\, to another mathematical problem that involves quaternion algebras. This result comes from a 2025 paper of ours\nhttps://indico.math.cnrs.fr/event/16282/
LOCATION:IHP\, 11 rue Pierre et Marie Curie\, Paris 5e
