DTEND:20260604T150000
SUMMARY:Darij Grinberg : Shuffles in the symmetric group algebra
DESCRIPTION:Ever since the famous 1992 work of Bayer and Diaconis\, it has been known that random shuffles of a deck of cards (with the back side up) can be modelled as elements of the group algebra $\\mathbb{R}[S_n]$ of the symmetric group $S_n$. This viewpoint has spawned progress in both card shuffling and the representation theory of the symmetric group. In this talk\, I will focus on two projects in the lat\nhttps://indico.math.cnrs.fr/event/16686/
LOCATION:IHP - Bâtiment Borel
URL:https://indico.math.cnrs.fr/event/16686/
END:VEVENT
